  ('zcrm_1579374000025016003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000026985001', 'Rachel Norton', NULL, '10-11-18 Rachel is 33 and husband is 31. She''s working as contractor right now and might get a job with benefits in future. Not sure. Her husband just got a job with benefits and it will still cost them about $833 a month ($10K per year) through his company. She also checked C4 for herself and it would be over $400. Our PSDHC option is around $269-$299 or so for one of them. She will discuss with husband and decide if one or both of them will join. We have follow up on Monday, Oct. 15th. She has asthma but not major and understands pre-x clause and she takes birth control. Husband doesn''t have anything to report. They see Dr. 1x or less per year not counting annual physical. She''s super happy to learn of this options and it takes much stress away to know there are some good options out there still.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2018-10-11 12:29:01', '2018-10-11 12:29:01'),
