  ('zcrm_1579374000021395028', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000044571112', 'Cheryl Claman-Brennan', NULL, '8-7-18 Wants to revisit this option. She''s 57. Sees primary care dr. 2-4x a year and lab work 1x year. Takes Gralise brand med which costs $700+ a month! Can''t source it through World Med RX but can get discount from co-pay network plan it appears. I told her in many numerous ways that her current shingles, post-repetic neuralgia, psychiatrist, therapist, acupuncture, massage, etc. are NOT going to be shared expenses at any point in time bc they are preventative/maintenance solutions. She also had a partial hysterectomy and has no cervix. So, that''s dealt with. Had colonoscopy at age 50 and doesn''t need one again until age 60. Doesn''t use chiro. Has a dependent who''s 24 in college and 21 dependent who is Not in school bc of disability. Another child 18 years old.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2018-08-08 16:51:36', '2018-08-08 16:51:36'),
