  ('zcrm_1579374000021288013', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000014508197', 'Jose Ernesto Rodriguez aleman', NULL, 'I called the billing department at Mayo clinic to ask about Ernesto, his upcoming apt on the 8th, and to ask about the $3,000 "deductible" that Joanna told us about.   I also asked Patricia if the $3,000 deductible came from the ASI card, and I explained that the $3,000-$6,000 did not apply to ASI, but is there so that our clients can use an HSA.  She said that the plan that they are on is considered a "Limited Benefits" plan and that the Mayo Clinic''s policy is to take a deposit before the exam, because they never know when a preventative care visit will turn into one filled with diagnostic/illness type tests.  I asked what type of visit did he book, that the deductible was $3,000?  She told me that she was not able to tell me the details, but that the $3,000 deposit was correct in amount for what twas scheduled.   She said that it is deposit, that they do bill ASI directly,  they will receive a refund depending on the conversation that they have with the Dr. what tests are run ect. - KC', 'Kelly Frederickson', 'Kelly Frederickson', '2018-08-03 10:14:49', '2018-08-03 10:14:49'),
