  ('zcrm_1579374000015736003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000011083254', 'Traci Reynolds', NULL, 'Received cancellation survey for this member.  Attached.  Will email ASi &amp; Sedera. Pmt cancelled in FTNI', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2018-04-12 07:28:37', '2018-04-12 07:35:28'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000015732003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000011521119', 'Kallie Carpenter', NULL, 'I spoke with Kallie right before close yesterday, I helped answer her questions on where she needs to send a new bill and why her birth control wasn''t being payed for per ASI, I told her that she will need to sit on the bill until we have time to thoroughly go over the new APEX that she now on, and that the birth control wasn''t being paid for because she was cancelled from ASI at the beginning of the month, I did however find a lower price on the birth control that she was quoted from her regular pharmacy- she asked if the birth control will be covered under APEX and I told her that we just do not know at this time. I sent her the coupon that I had found- KC', 'Kelly Frederickson', 'Kelly Frederickson', '2018-04-12 07:13:12', '2018-04-12 07:13:12'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000015703185', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000000165429', 'Jodie Brenner', NULL, '4-11-18 Jodie is considering cancelling our HES portion since hasn''t really used it and looking to lower costs. But, I explained all aspects and she''s going to ponder if it''s worthwhile. She called in once and asked for assistance in finding a new Dr. in MT and John gave her the link to Healthgrades which she was already looking at herself so didn''t feel the value in that. She''s didn''t know about telemedicine or QR code. So, again pondering its worth to her. She still needs to update her cc to keep it going.  She''s already updated it with LHS. She''s interested in exploring new options in Nov. She might want a more traditional option that feels more guaranteed and allows for tax benefits since she''s self employed and own own home now. I then mentioned our new Association plan with the co-pay option and cost would be about $331 or $381 for the $500 or $1000 IUA. That piqued her interest having the set co-pays for those items with Apex and the tax benefits. She asked me to send her information in June when that program is available.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2018-04-11 15:09:03', '2018-04-11 15:11:07'),
