  ('zcrm_1579374000014263062', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000060163052', 'Rita Boccuzzi', NULL, '3-5-18 Husband is smoker and too risky to include him! He will stay on Kaiser or regular plan.  Son will go on employer plan that he only has to pay $90 for. She might chose this if her records are clear from any major red flags.  Nasal Congestion = Allergic Rhinitis. Anxiety in 2013 gone. Allergies never treated. Nerve damage permanent in ear, 40% hearing loss, no meds, no treatment, 160 and 5''1. Nasal drip. 2012 in remission for cancer but records show wrong as 2017. She''s going to ask to Attending Physician''s Update on her records to show them accurately. They have all sorts of mistakes, dates and misrepresentation. Also showing hysterectomy which is not true since still has ovaries but the Kaiser system didn''t allow for another way to label it so they kept it as such. Ridiculous. She''ll call me if/when the records are fixed and she has no major concerns.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2018-03-05 17:14:24', '2018-03-05 17:27:11'),
