  ('zcrm_1579374000013602003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000011881395', 'Elaine Rampone', NULL, 'Welcome call completed.  Member not aware IUA is per incident.  Thought it was a deductible.', 'MPB Health Member Notification', 'MPB Health Member Notification', '2018-02-16 08:35:55', '2018-02-16 08:35:55'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000013591003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000013590042', 'Donald J. Hinz Jr.', NULL, 'Emp Only $1000 IUA', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2018-02-16 07:06:21', '2018-02-16 07:06:21'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000013576015', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000019362116', 'Natasha Thompson', NULL, '2-15-18 She is looking to make a change with work. Might only earn $500 a month. But, then asked me to quote at $55K per year which is too much for subsidy. Priced out cheapest plan for her at $325 with Kaiser for worst plan and $249/$299 for HEP. She Might be married if that helps or might file taxes separately. She is 36 and healthy, no pre-x tobacco, drugs or anything. Will contact me when she had a better idea of what she will do moving forward.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2018-02-15 16:20:41', '2018-02-15 16:21:24'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000013576003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000016038124', 'Isabelle Laak', NULL, '2-15-18 From France and has ins. thru employer but doesn''t like it. Paying about $300 for her husband and not sure how much for her. Employer contributing 100% of her cost. She thinks they will gladly contribute to this instead. They are pretty healthy, she''s a massage therapist who is also friends with ND and other docs who are tired of the industry and just feel like sales people and can''t help the sick or injured. She wants to share this with them. She has a friend whose husband was on a health sharing membership last year and died of pancreatic cancer. All the bills were paid and it totally worked! She was astonished. She already has an HSA plan. She had a great quote! "This brings human dignity back!" And she later said "I feel like a butterfly with wings." after explaining concept. She had a friend who plays poker and has tons of cash. The friend needed a surgery which was going to cost $30K. He told the hospital he didn''t have insurance and he''d pay in cash. They said ok until he tried to hand them the cash. The wouldn''t accept his cash payment! They wrote it off and refused his payment. This happened 10 years ago.
Her company has to renew their policy in May which might be an opportunity to offer this to the group. Isabelle knows of deadline for Feb. and might wind up going with April 1st start to give herself time to absorb it all and talk with employer.  She will contact me in a week or so.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2018-02-15 14:48:41', '2018-02-15 14:48:41'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000013568003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000011919812', 'Mary Beth Hassett', NULL, 'client called with a question about registering for Teledoc,  I walked her through the whole process, but it seemed to be a glitch on her end, so I gave her the phone number for Teledoc support service. KC', 'Kelly Frederickson', 'Kelly Frederickson', '2018-02-15 12:35:52', '2018-02-15 12:35:52'),
