  ('zcrm_1579374000012909021', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000011521350', 'Shane Michael Sorensen', NULL, '1-31-18 Trudi did her annual wellness visit last week and hadn''t received the MEC+ card yet to told them she''s a self-pay patient. She didn''t realize about the 90 day requested wait. He bill as self pay was $300+. I told her to ask for John''s help with that bill during their Welcome Call on Wed. Feb. 7th that is scheduled. They will both be on the call as well and ask the rest of their questions at that time. Super nice about it all.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2018-01-31 11:42:41', '2018-01-31 11:42:41'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000012907015', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000012935161', 'Jill St. Aubin King', NULL, 'Emp &amp; Sp $1000 IUA', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2018-01-31 10:26:37', '2018-01-31 10:26:37'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000012907009', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000012935075', 'Fabiola Gomes', NULL, 'Emp Only $1000 IUA', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2018-01-31 10:16:24', '2018-01-31 10:16:24'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000012909009', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000012935161', 'Jill St. Aubin King', NULL, '1-31-18 Choosing $1000/$485 for her and her husband. Enrolling right now.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2018-01-31 10:12:06', '2018-01-31 10:12:06'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000012909003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000012935161', 'Jill St. Aubin King', NULL, '1-23-18 A client of mine gave me your contact information and my husband and I are very interested in the Sedera program. The “layers” approach makes perfect sense to us and we are thrilled to have an alternative solution to our current situation. I do have some initial questions though, particularly about the HSA. 

We are self employed and currently have a HDHP/HSA on the Colorado exchange. The current cost of our HDHP is unaffordable (more than our mortgage) though we like the HSA approach. If I understand the Sedera program correctly, we are encouraged, not required, to have a MEC policy to participate? Does your program offer an option to purchase MEC coverage to keep our current HSA or is this coverage something we need to find independently? Do you have resources for this coverage? Do we have the option of not having the MEC while maintaining membership? 

Also, we currently have our three children covered on a traditional policy. We don’t anticipate adding them but in the event their insurance becomes unaffordable I had a couple of questions. My youngest daughter has type 1 juvenile diabetes. Would the pre existing condition be covered after a certain point or would she be denied coverage? 

Lots of questions that may be better asked/answered via phone conversation. Please feel free to call me at your convenience. My cell is 303-709-6080. 

Jill St.Aubin King 
Co-Owner, Monarch Gardens 
