  ('zcrm_1579374000012896003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000019634002', 'Colleen Mangeot', NULL, '1-23-18 Teresa Robertson gave me your name and sent me a link to some information on Sedera.   

My husband and I are currently covered under my employer’s plan.  It is a high deductible plan with claims paid by Anthem, though they are self insured.  My husband is retiring next month and turns 65 Jan 2019.  I will be 58 in March and anticipate quitting my job around June, when we expect to relocate to our home in Asheville NC.  Hence, we will both need health insurance at that time.  

In reading through the materials, it sounds like we need to have a business in order to qualify for Sedera.  While my husband is selling is 50% ownership in a business at retirement, we will still own 50% of B & D Properties, a company that owns a building that is rented to another business.   Will we qualify to purchase insurance through Sedera?  Will the other person who owns the other 50% of B & D properties be affected in anyway, if we choose Sedera, but he does not?  

If we are able to qualify, other than reading through more of the materials, is there another step I should be taking?  

Thank you!

Colleen"', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2018-01-30 15:20:26', '2018-01-30 15:20:26'),
